  result: The sole current Companion wire is loopback-capability/4 plus acquire.v2, operation.v3, and operation-projection.v2. It requires one explicit attempt, the exact pinned Qwen3 source and corrected composition profile /4, source-only route, private create-only execution/source evidence whose intent and receipt bind one canonical nine-file payload inventory, independent browser and managed enforcement of the same source constants, pairwise nonoverlapping custody roots, authoritative create-only history with current-cache lag bounded to one record and repaired under both locks before another append, reclaimed exact-key mutation gates, a bounded five-second cancellation mutation wait, monotonic terminal state, and exact six-member fixed-chunk transfer. Superseded request/operation/projection readers, arbitrary inventory digests, and fake peer states are absent from the current executable path.
  verification: Managed Release solution 252/252 with Companion 125, Core 86, and package boundary 41; warnings as errors and format gate pass; focused browser/vector 19/19; standard Node partition 1702 pass, zero fail, three declared skips, 1705 total; diff hygiene passes.
  release_truth: The listener still returns typed operation-not-available, no production operation executor or source-network owner exists, the browser client is not loaded by the product UI, and no real source, conversion, model, browser chat, P2P, deployment, publication, or live MemoryEndpoints evidence exists.
  next_gate: Implement the preregistered exclusive restart-safe source operation owner, bounded pinned-source streaming, contained converter launch, and terminal six-member inspection before wiring listener routes or deleting the superseded UI bridge in one later green clean cut.
  memory_policy: MemoryEndpoints is authorized and strongly recommended for portable continuity; configured or reachable state is not authenticated live lifecycle evidence.
  campaign_truth: 0/20 qualified; 0/50 browser; 0/25 live memory; 0/40 outside lanes; 0/20 catalog.

