active_enterprise_intake_clean_cut_rule_2026_08_28: Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-enterprise-intake-and-production-runtime-clean-cut-memory-2026-08-28.md`, 20,316 bytes/SHA256 `6e5a5b7cf7f3ad45008b14597a3616ee603da76cc500b69770de7280711785e4`, before TinyRustLM architecture, SLM2, tokenizer/template/sampling/prompt, runtime, WASM, browser worker, acquisition/companion, quality/training, memory/MemoryEndpoints, P2P, release, documentation, OMI, Colibri, TurboVec, or TurboQuant work. It consolidates 344 files in 23 manifest-owned batches; follow its manifest and ledger routes instead of bulk-loading raw reports. One exact six-member composition and one Rust/worker path are authoritative. Reports advise only. The current blocker is browser companion/acquisition replacement and deletion, then full verification; earlier missing-worker-manifest/scalar-identity status is superseded.
