memory_strategy:
  hot_memory: .uai/
  durable_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/ and docs/ deep-linked from .uai/long-term-memory.uai
  public_durable_target: https://aiwikis.org/runtime-mirust/
  note: LLM Wiki and docs-based durable Markdown are both valid when deep-linked from .uai with routing summaries and review status.
  split_memory_architecture_rule: Hot `.uai` memory remains active startup, current-state, handoff, and operational memory even when durable wiki, docs, database, or NeuralWikis-style memory exists; durable memory augments `.uai` and must not retire, replace, ignore, or make `.uai` emergency-only.
  hot_memory_current_state_rule: Keep hot `.uai` compact and current-state oriented; store bulky dated evidence, report bodies, and historical proof in docs/wiki/report-intake and route it through checksum-bearing pointers.
  hot_report_synthesis: .uai/report-synthesis.uai must summarize processed reports enough for cold-start routing before durable wiki loading.
  hot_short_term_report_pointer: .uai/short-term-memory.uai must reference current report-intake indexes and durable synthesis nodes after each processed handoff batch.
  site_voice_hot_memory: .uai/taboo.uai governs public copy and product positioning for this website.
  dogfood_rule: If durable wiki memory is hard to crawl from .uai, update UAIX/LLM Wiki guidance and strengthen hot .uai synthesis rather than only adding more Markdown.
  report_storage_rule: Keep report bodies in wiki/raw durable evidence, keep short-term memory as current routing plus proof pointers, and keep long-term memory as checksum-bearing pointers.
  short_term_report_routes_rule: .uai/short-term-memory.uai must expose current_report_routes for report indexes, durable research, active bucket disposition, UAIX strategy source, and the long-term pointer ledger.
  uaix_file_handoff_strategy_source: https://uaix.org/en-us/tools/ai-memory-package-wizard/#setup-file-handoff
  uaix_file_handoff_strategy_2026_06_27: Scan active buckets first, record disposition and proof-of-use, preserve originals with checksums in durable evidence, synthesize durable wiki/report/docs nodes, refresh hot routing, audit long-term pointers, then remove processed source-site copies unless a named keep-active exception or blocker is recorded.
  uaix_file_handoff_strategy_2026_06_28: Apply setup-file-handoff as a cold-start loop: active buckets are intake, raw/wiki files hold durable bodies, `.uai` files hold routing and synthesis, short-term memory names current report/research routes, and long-term memory keeps checksum pointers.
  report_pointer_audit_2026_06_27: Every current wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/*.md report page is represented in .uai/long-term-memory.uai; future report pages must be added to that ledger and routed from short-term memory.
  report_pointer_audit_2026_06_28: Every current report and research page must stay represented in .uai/long-term-memory.uai and referenced from .uai/short-term-memory.uai after report, research, dogfood, or strategy refresh work.
  research_reference_distribution_rule: Keep research/reference bodies in wiki/runtime-mirust/research/ and report syntheses in wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/; route them from short-term memory and checksum-bearing long-term pointers instead of inlining them into long-term memory.
  runtime_rebrand_2026_06_30: Route Runtime.MiRust.com site identity, `runtime-mirust` wiki/raw namespaces, publish-review bundle naming, old-name audits, and outer folder handoff through wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/runtime-rebrand-memory-2026-06-30.md.
